.SH SYNOPSIS
dropdmg [options] file...

dropdmg \-\-burn\-image file...

dropdmg \-\-burn\-file file...

dropdmg \-\-version


.SH DESCRIPTION
The dropdmg tool lets you use the command line to create disk images and
archives with DropDMG. If you specify no options, DropDMG will create a plain
zlib\-compressed .dmg image.

The output is the paths to the created files/folders.

Names of configurations, licenses, and layouts are case\-sensitive.


.SH OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0

.TP
.BI \-\-config\-name\fn= <name> ,\ \-g
The name of a collection of DropDMG settings. If this parameter is
specified, it overrides the other parameters. If "" is specified, uses the
current configuration chosen in the preferences.


.TP
.B \-\-always\-create , \-t
Wrap a disk image or archive using the specified format, rather than
converting.


.TP
.BI \-\-format\fn= <format> ,\ \-f
zlib, bzip2, lzfse, ro, sparsebundle, sparseimage, rw, tar.gz, tar.bz2, tar, zip,
master, hybrid, ndif, ndifro, ndifrw


.TP
.BI \-\-encryption\fn= <encryptionType> ,\ \-c
none, aes\-128, aes\-256


.TP
.BI \-\-passphrase\fn= <passphrase> ,\ \-h
The passphrase for an encrypted image. Prompts if you use \-c without \-h.


.TP
.BI \-\-segment\-size\fn= <megabytes> ,\ \-s
0 means don\'t segment. (defaults to 0)


.TP
.BI \-\-layout\-name\fn= <name> ,\ \-y
The name of a layout in the preferences window.


.TP
.BI \-\-layout\-folder\fn= <folder>
The path to a layout folder stored outside DropDMG (e.g. under version
control) created by dragging from the preferences window to the Finder.


.TP
.BI \-\-APP_BASENAME\fn= <value>
The value for the \fB${APP_BASENAME}\fP variable in the layout.


.TP
.BI \-\-APP_SHORT_VERSION_STRING\fn= <value>
The value for the \fB${APP_SHORT_VERSION_STRING}\fP variable in the layout.


.TP
.BI \-\-APP_VERSION\fn= <value>
The value for the \fB${APP_VERSION}\fP variable in the layout.


.TP
.BI \-\-license\-name\fn= <name> ,\ \-l
The name of a license in the preferences window.


.TP
.BI \-\-license\-folder\fn= <folder>
The path to a license folder stored outside DropDMG (e.g. under version
control) created by dragging from the preferences window to the Finder.


.TP
.B \-\-custom\-icon , \-n
Customize the icon of the mounted image.


.TP
.B \-\-internet\-enabled , \-i
(defaults to false)


.TP
.B \-\-append\-current\-date
Append the current date to the name of the output file? (defaults to false)


.TP
.B \-\-append\-version\-number
Append the version number of the application being imaged to the name of the output file? (defaults to false)


.TP
.B \-\-optimize\-for\-restores , \-r
(defaults to false)


.TP
.B \-\-sanitize\-for\-servers
Replace spaces and non\-ASCII characters in the file name? (defaults to
false)


.TP
.BI \-\-base\-name\fn= <basename> ,\ \-b
"" means automatic. (defaults to "")


.TP
.BI \-\-volume\-name\fn= <volumeName> ,\ \-v
"" means automatic. (defaults to "")


.TP
.BI \-\-destination\fn= <folder> ,\ \-o
If absent, the destination is next to the source.


.TP
.B \-\-delete\-original , \-d
(defaults to false)

.UNINDENT

.SH EXAMPLES
Create plain zlib images from two folders:

.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
dropdmg ~/my\-folder ~/my\-other\-folder

.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
Convert a .dmg image into a .tar.bz2 archive:

.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
dropdmg \-\-format tar.bz2 ~/my\-image.dmg

.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
Create an encrypted image with password "bar" that is internet\-enabled:

.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
dropdmg \-c aes\-128 \-h bar \-i ~/my\-folder

.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
Burn the contents of a disk image to CD/DVD:

.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
dropdmg \-\-burn\-image ~/Desktop/image.dmg

.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
Burn the contents of a folder to CD/DVD:

.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
dropdmg \-\-burn\-file ~/Desktop/folder

.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
Find out the version of the dropdmg tool:

.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
dropdmg \-\-version

.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT

